  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 12/02/2025, the proposed sub-division of the dwellinghouse and part change of use of '1 Albert Road, Hounslow, TW3 3RW' from Use Class C3(a) to Use Class C3(b) was not lawful within the meaning of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended) because:\r\n1.\tThe proposed subdivision of the single dwellinghouse into two separate residential units constitutes a material change of use and requires full planning permission (Section 55(3a) of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990).\r\n2.\tThe applicant has failed to submit sufficient information to demonstrate that the proposal pertaining to the part change of use of the application site from Use class C3(a) to C3(b) would not result in a material change of use of the site under Section 55 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended). Planning permission is therefore required.\r\n"
  ],
